#
# The shell has no device tree node, so every chain starts from a node found by
# its compatible string: the firmware node, which links to the mailbox, and the
# power management node. The shell switches the LED through the mailbox and
# resets the board through the power component. It draws in a window of the
# compositor, a program in the same image; the lava lamp follows the window's
# focus on the interface's io-channel, and asks `snapshot` for it when it
# starts and after records were dropped.
uses mailbox_v1 via device compatible "raspberrypi,bcm2835-firmware", mboxes { set_led }
uses power_v1 via device compatible "brcm,bcm2835-pm" { reset }
uses compositor_v1 via component compositor { pixel_order, create_window, commit, move_window, raise, destroy, snapshot }
